      },
      "text": "Punta Arenas to King George Island"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:5a4836cca1208c95",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "3f32559809a503a13258d4aa769dd69b456155b0ea1ee337af55d42db7bc1732",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-f8804ba1-147d-4106-9470-50bbc2568386",
        "model": "ChatGPT"
      },
      "text": "A transfer will take you from your hotel to Punta Arenas Airport for the flight to King George Island in Antarctica.\n\nOn arrival, your guide will meet the group. The day’s programme includes:\n\n- Villa Las Estrellas, a Chilean settlement on King George Island.\n- The Russian Orthodox church at Bellingshausen Station.\n- A Zodiac trip to Ardley Island and a visit to the penguin colony.\n- A boat trip to Collins Glacier.\n\nAfter the day’s excursions, you’ll be taken to the ice camp on Collins Glacier, about 6 km from the runway.\n\nThe camp has an insulated tent that serves as a shared dining room, a separate tent housing the main toilet, and three small insulated sleeping tents. Each sleeping tent accommodates three to six people.\n\nOvernight at the ice camp on King George Island."
    },
